From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:22:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: apple,s8000-mca: Add the T7001 MCA

The iPad Air 2 (A8X, T7001) has the MCA in its "mca-version 1" form: the
fields of the A9/A10 MCA at the older A5-era register offsets. Its
speaker link (MCA3, two MAX98721 amplifiers in TDM slots) runs with the
MCA as clock provider from an AP NCO channel, like the T8010 speaker
link, and takes a single playback DMA channel. Name it apple,t7001-mca.

The NCO runs at twice the bit clock on this version (iOS forces an
MCLK/SCLK ratio of at least two); say so in the clock description.

Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml  | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
index b9eda41..b17cd99 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Apple S8000/T8010 MCA I2S controller
+title: Apple T7001/S8000/T8010 MCA I2S controller
 
 maintainers:
   - Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
@@ -18,7 +18,10 @@ description: |
   with an AP NCO bitclock: apple,t8010-mca is the playback-only digital
   speaker link (TDM), apple,t8010-mca-i2s the playback-only stereo I2S link
   to the headphone codec. The MCAs are the same block; the compatible names
-  the link setup iOS programs into it.
+  the link setup iOS programs into it. The T7001 (A8X) MCA is the older
+  "mca-version 1" register layout with the same fields: apple,t7001-mca is
+  the playback-only speaker link (TDM) of the iPad Air 2, clocked from an AP
+  NCO channel running at twice the bit clock.
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: dai-common.yaml#
@@ -26,6 +29,7 @@ allOf:
       properties:
         compatible:
           enum:
+            - apple,t7001-mca
             - apple,t8010-mca
             - apple,t8010-mca-i2s
     then:
@@ -46,12 +50,15 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
       - apple,s8000-mca
+      - apple,t7001-mca
       - apple,t8010-mca
       - apple,t8010-mca-i2s
 
   clocks:
     maxItems: 1
-    description: AP NCO channel supplying the T8010 bitclock
+    description:
+      AP NCO channel supplying the bitclock (T7001, T8010). On T7001 the
+      MCA divides it by two.
 
   clock-names:
     const: bitclk
